From bc6002d0daf4189f13aaf5dbc1822eb65757bf70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arham Mahajan <mahajanarham0@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:46:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(acp): opt into shared router effort discovery for T3

Keep the standard model-specific thought_level control by default. The T3 provider can opt into an uncategorized union of published efforts so its single-model probe makes the control available across the catalog. Validate selections against the active model and block prompts after a rejected effort to prevent silent fallback. Cover shared discovery, independent model state, unknown vocabularies, and recovery.
